    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i know what i did, but that was then. that version of me had a mission. now i'm just... waiting. it's like i finished the book and i'm just staring at the blank pages at the end. it feels so heavy, like i'm just taking up space that someone else could actually use. does that even make sense?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is a heavy and common feeling to lose the \"mission\" that once gave every morning a sense of purpose after a long, difficult life. The \"end of a book\" moment often triggers a grief so deep it feels like the ending is permanent, but many find that the next page is just blank because the story is now about self-discovery, not just fixing others. You are taking up the space of a person who has done the ultimate good, and the silence is just the quiet before a life that no one else can live in your absence.",
